Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:01:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ps4: a joystick driver for the DualShock 4

The controller of each user logged in (libScePad), one joystick per login
slot, which is its player index, named after the user. It is a DualShock 4
to SDL (Sony's vendor and product ids), with buttons and axes laid out as
the HIDAPI driver lays them out on a PC, and a game controller mapping from
the driver. Sticks and triggers are linear, from 0..255 to -32768..32767.

The PS and SHARE buttons belong to the system: there is no guide and no
back button, and the touch pad click is the touchpad button. The touch pad
(two fingers), the gyroscope and the accelerometer, rumble and the light
bar are supported; the light bar goes back to the user's color, and rumble
stops, when the joystick is closed. A controller that goes away has its
joystick recentered until it is back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
